    "result": "I added `Cancel` in `job.go`. I could not run the tests: `go test` needs your approval here.\n\nThe three booleans (`Running`, `Done`, `Failed`) are gone. In their place is one `State` value and a table of allowed moves between states. Done, failed and cancelled have no moves out, so they are final. Every method checks the move against that table, so a late `Succeed` or `Fail` after `Cancel` returns `ErrState` and changes nothing. The limit of 3 attempts and the `Status` strings work as before.\n\nCAUTION: this changes the public API. Code that reads or sets `j.Running`, `j.Done` or `j.Failed` will no longer compile. `Attempts` is still exported.\n\nI also added `job_test.go`. It covers retrying until failed, cancelling a waiting or running job, a late `Succeed`/`Fail`, and `Cancel` on a finished job.\n\n**TLDR**\n`Cancel` is in `job.go`. The three booleans are replaced by one state and a table of allowed moves, which breaks code that uses those fields. The new tests in `job_test.go` have not run: `go test ./...` needs your approval.",
